  "method": "Direct original Action + action_slot on target, sampled every integer frame inclusive at 24 fps. Tear diagnostic measures separation of pairs coincident within a 0.1 micrometre rounded grid in rest pose. Edge strain uses edges of at least 0.5 mm rest length, with hip zone within 80 mm and shoulder, elbow and knee zones within 55 mm of bilateral pivots. Wrist strain uses both rest-space x strips from 245 to 345 mm lateral. An intact shared edge can stretch without creating a seam. Renders use the complete imported target, its materials, orthographic three-quarter views and Cycles CPU. Both the untouched local-quaternion assignment and source-to-target world-rest-basis transfer are evaluated. Images show direct binding if all 25 nonfinger frames differ by under 0.1 degree, otherwise the transfer. Local joint translations are converted through the corresponding 3x3 rest-basis transformation. Only evaluation changes; no retargeted Action is saved in either delivered asset.",
